---
import { withBase } from '../config/site.mjs';
---
<section class="receipt-section wrap" aria-labelledby="receipt-title">
  <div class="section-heading receipt-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The run</p><h2 id="receipt-title">One request<br /><span>through the yard.</span></h2><p>The operator asks for a retry fix that reaches production code. Railyard binds the outcome to a route, implementation lane, review packet, and delivery tail. The turn is the evidence decision: findings return to the work, while settled evidence earns merge authority. The run closes when merge ancestry and a focused post-merge check are visible. <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/delivery/model-routing/worked-runs/')}>Read a complete routed run.</a></p></div>
  <div class="terminal" aria-label="Illustrative chat transcript for an agent delivery">
    <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>railyard / receipt</b></div>
    <div class="terminal-body">
      <p class="speaker">you</p>
      <p><mark>“Ship the retry fix and get it merged.”</mark></p>
      <p class="muted">routing <span>implementation</span> · effort max</p>
      <p><b class="check">✓</b> plan → implementation → review</p>
      <p><b class="check">✓</b> independent correctness + quality lenses</p>
      <p><b class="check">✓</b> <a href={withBase('/delivery/gates/#merge-settlement')}>pull request checks settled</a></p>
      <p><b class="check">✓</b> merge reachable from <code>main</code></p>
      <p class="receipt-result"><span>post-merge proof</span><strong>verified</strong></p>
      <p class="terminal-note">Illustrative transcript. Actual usage is a chat request to your agent, not a shell command.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
